# Meltdown — Overview

SCAFFOLD. This file is a placeholder created by the scaffold stage so the
manifest resolves; the specification stage replaces it in full.

Scope this file owns, and nothing else:

What the game is and what the finished build must be: the premise; the hard requirements (real graphics, no backend, no keys, the npm build interface, a README, the instrumentation deliverable, the toolchain commands); the code-quality requirement stated beside the checks that must pass; the free choices; the fixed 1280 x 720 stage and its two regions; the centre convention for every reported (x, y); the stage-fit requirement; the legibility table; what is out of scope. It states the stage and the centre convention, then names specs/floor.md as where the tile-to-stage map lives. Branches on engine.slug.
